preConditionHook:
// THE STOP SITS AT ONE SPECIFIC BAR'S EXTREME, not at a window's. A long is
// closed when the close reaches the low of the bar exactly nBarsAgo bars back;
// the short mirrors on that bar's high. Grimes G08-14, "stop out at the lowest
// low of three days ago".
//
// NOT A TRUE TRAIL. Because the anchor is one bar and not a Lowest() window,
// the level is NOT monotone: as the window rolls, a lower bar arriving at
// offset nBarsAgo LOOSENS the stop again. That is the whole difference from
// StopBeyondRecentRangeExtreme, and it is why the single-bar reading was kept
// rather than folded into that rule.
//
// Degenerate overlap, recorded not resolved: at nBarsAgo = 1 this is
// TrailArmedAfterProfitThreshold at armProfitDollars 0 / stopOffsetTicks 0
// (MaxPositionProfit starts at 0, so that arming is always true). The grid
// should start at 2.
//
// nBarsAgo is a double input, so the subscript narrows -- deliberate, as
// README "Input variables" says.
//
// Deepest bar touched: nBarsAgo.
